source:
(all under OmniGibson's friction: coefficient 0.2 on revolute, 0.3 on prismatic joints of scene objects):
  handle  constant horizontal force at the handle (or the panel's free edge without one), perpendicular to the panel, held
          1 s from closed at 200 Hz physics with the robot held still; per door the smallest force of the grid that turns
          it 0.3 rad (a hinge) or moves it 0.05 rad / 0.05 m within 1 s:
          door_force probes (grid 2,3,5,7,10,15,20,30,50,80,120,200,300 N) and
          door_turn probes (grid 2,5,10,20,30,50,80,120,200,300 N); file: each probe's output;
  edge    "legacy" (= OmniGibson's friction) rows: force ramp 10 N/s at the free edge (breakaway), smallest constant edge
          force of 2,3,5,7,10,15,20,30,50,80 N that turns a hinge 0.3 rad or slides a slide 0.1 m in 1 s (along a sliding
          door's track), from friction probes in canning_food;
  sweep   legacy breakaway at the handle and free edge for every door class of 6 scenes;
  pulls   room doors pulled toward the robot by hand: physical pinch (physpull probe, legacy rows), assisted
          attachment at the handle (door_open probe, tidying_bathroom);
  push    walking chest-first into a door that swings away (pushdoor probe, legacy rows, 8 s;
          pushdoor_long probe, 30 s);
  hands   horizontal force on the standing robot's hand(s) along its heading (hand_force probe);
  release released doors (canning_food) and drawers (drawer_release probe, legacy rows);
  level   lids and drop-down doors on level hinges released part-way (canning_food, legacy rows).
